<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 January, from 1018 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1018">1018 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,008 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry II and Bolesław I make the Peace of Bautzen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Henry II and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen">Peace of Bautzen</a>, ending fifteen years of intermittent war over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. Poland kept Lusatia and Milsko, and German knights later joined Bolesław's expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen">Peace of Bautzen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1287">1287 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">739 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wareru proclaims himself king of Martaban as Pagan collapses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wareru">Wareru</a>, a Mon of humble origin, declared himself king of Martaban as the Pagan Kingdom collapsed, and Pagan, in its death throes, took no action. His kingdom, later called Hanthawaddy, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a> until 1539.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wareru">Wareru</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1649">1649 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">377 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles I is beheaded in Whitehall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Convicted of treason, Charles I was executed on a scaffold outside the Banqueting House. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> became a republic, and the monarchy was not restored until 1660.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson survives an assassination attempt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the US <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a>, the house painter Richard Lawrence fired two pistols at Jackson, but both misfired. It was the first known attempt to kill a sitting American president.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1882">1882 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Franklin D. Roosevelt is born at Hyde Park, New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roosevelt led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a> and most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. He is the only president elected four times.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler appointed Chancellor of Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Hindenburg made the Nazi leader Chancellor, with conservatives expecting to control him. Within months Hitler had suspended civil liberties and established a one-party dictatorship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet submarine sinks the Wilhelm Gustloff</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Torpedoes from submarine S-13 sank the overcrowded German liner in the Baltic as it evacuated refugees and military personnel. An estimated 9,000 died, the greatest loss of life in a single sinking.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mahatma Gandhi is assassinated in New Delhi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nationalist Nathuram Godse shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> at a prayer meeting at Birla House. The death of the leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s non-violent independence struggle was mourned across the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tet Offensive begins in South Vietnam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">North Vietnamese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-cong">Viet Cong</a> forces attacked towns and bases across South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> during the lunar new year truce. Though repelled, the offensive undermined American confidence in the war.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 January <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-frederick-margrave-of-baden-durlach"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-frederick-margrave-of-baden-durlach.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Frederick, Margrave of Baden-Durlach</span><span class="tp">1573–1638</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/franklin-d-roosevelt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franklin-d-roosevelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Franklin D. Roosevelt</span><span class="tp">1882–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/s-n-goenka"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">S. N. Goenka</span><span class="tp">1924–2013</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/islam-karimov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/islam-karimov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Islam Karimov</span><span class="tp">1938–2016</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ii-of-jordan"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Abdullah II of Jordan</span><span class="tp">b. 1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/felipe-vi-of-spain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/felipe-vi-of-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Felipe VI of Spain</span><span class="tp">b. 1968</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 January <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-montagu-1st-earl-of-salisbury"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-montagu-1st-earl-of-salisbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury</span><span class="tp">1301–1344</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-count-of-flanders"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-ii-count-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis II, Count of Flanders</span><span class="tp">1330–1384</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-i-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles I of England</span><span class="tp">1600–1649</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/osceola"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/osceola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Osceola</span><span class="tp">1804–1838</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
